    "result": "Excellent! All tests now pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### 1. **Fixed APPROVAL_STATUSES export** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was expecting to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available through the default export\n   - This fixed the governance test error: `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')`\n\n### 2. **Fixed toxicity metric evaluation** (`src/eval/index.js`)\n   - Modified `runEvaluations` to handle `toxicityMetric` specially by only passing the outputs, not the references\n   - The issue was that `toxicityMetric` has a different signature than other metrics\u2014it accepts `(outputs, bannedTerms)` with defaults to `defaultBannedTerms`\n   - When called with `(outputs, references)`, the references were being used as banned terms, causing false positives\n   - This fixed the eval test error: `expected +0 to be 1`\n\nAll 28 tests now pass successfully while maintaining backward compatibility with existing public exports.",
